  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing maximum\nnicotine levels for electronic cigarettes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6076",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6076-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 52,
       "fullName": "Fredrick J. Akshar II",
       "imgName": "735_Fredrick_Akshar.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 913,
       "sessionMemberId": 1381,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "AKSHAR"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1399-aa & 1399-dd, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6076\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing maxi-\nmum nicotine levels for electronic cigarettes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nSets maximum nicotine level of 2% for e-liquids manufactured in New York\nand makes violations of the limit a civil penalty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends section 1399-aa of the Public Health Law by defining\nthe term 'e-liquid.'\n\nSection 2. amends section 1399-dd of the Public Health law by limiting\nnicotine levels in e-liquids manufactured in New York to a maximum of 2%\nand imposes a civil penalty for each violation.\n\nSection 3. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nE-cigarettes and vaping products are often billed as a healthier\nreplacement for cigarettes. Yet the nicotine content of many vaping\nproducts is poorly regulated and has no established legal nicotine\nlimit. It is a common-sense requirement that the amount of highly addic-\ntive chemicals remain below set limits.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or\nrepeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the implementation of\nthis act on its effective date are authorized to be made and completed\non or before such effective date.\n",
